# Toggle switches, not checkboxes

For any boolean on/off setting in the UI, use the shared `Switch` component from `src/ui/Switch.tsx`. Do not use `<input type="checkbox">`.

## Use Switch when

- Enabling or disabling a feature (MythicRPG add-on, auto-save, resource bar)
- Yes/no options in wizards and settings
- Any control that is switchable on its own (not one choice among many)

## Prefer this pattern

```tsx
import { Switch } from '../Switch'

<div className="wz-toggle">
  <span className="wz-toggle-copy">
    <span className="wz-toggle-title">Global</span>
    <span className="wz-toggle-hint">Every player has this reagent</span>
  </span>
  <Switch
    checked={value}
    onChange={setValue}
    aria-label="Global"
  />
</div>
```

Or the compact Settings / NewPack row style with a label beside `<Switch checked={...} onChange={...} />`.

## Do not use Switch for

- Exclusive multi-option choices (use radio buttons, segmented chips, or a select)
- Multi-select lists of items (use chips, lists, or dedicated multi-select UI)

## Bad

```tsx
<label>
  <input type="checkbox" checked={on} onChange={(e) => setOn(e.target.checked)} />
  Enable feature
</label>
```

## Good

```tsx
<Switch checked={on} onChange={setOn} aria-label="Enable feature" />
```
